# Evaluation Scenarios — observing-oci-java-functions

## Scenario 1: Instrument a New Java Function with Metrics and Structured Logs

```json
{
  "skills": ["observing-oci-java-functions"],
  "query": "I need to add observability to a new OCI Java function — it should post a custom metric for each successful and failed order, and log all events as structured JSON.",
  "expected_behavior": [
    "Uses ResourcePrincipalAuthenticationDetailsProvider — no hardcoded API keys or PEM files",
    "Initializes MonitoringClient in @FnConfiguration or static block (not inside handleRequest)",
    "Writes structured JSON logs to System.out (not unstructured println)",
    "Calls postMetricData synchronously inside handleRequest before returning",
    "Uses PostMetricDataDetails.BatchAtomicity.NonAtomic",
    "Reads COMPARTMENT_OCID and METRIC_NAMESPACE from RuntimeContext.getConfigurationByKey",
    "Catches observability exceptions without rethrowing — observability failure does not fail the function",
    "Generates a pom.xml that imports oci-java-sdk-bom:3.87.0 in dependencyManagement"
  ]
}
```

