## Scenario 2: Choose a Distributed Tracing Strategy for a Multi-Function Chain

```json
{
  "skills": ["observing-oci-java-functions"],
  "query": "We have three OCI Java Functions that call each other in a chain. We want to see end-to-end traces in OCI APM. Cold-start must stay under 1 second. We don't need portability to other backends.",
  "expected_behavior": [
    "Presents the tracing strategy decision matrix before generating code (OCI APM Agent, OTel Agent, Manual SDK, None)",
    "Recommends OCI APM Java Agent or OpenTelemetry Agent given the cold-start budget > 800ms is feasible",
    "Flags cold-start impact for each option (+80–150ms for APM agent, +120–200ms for OTel agent)",
    "Confirms use of APM Private Data Key (not Public Data Key) for server-side functions",
    "Shows APM_PRIVATE_DATA_KEY injected via function config — never hardcoded",
    "Notes that OTLP endpoint URL must be retrieved from OCI Console, not constructed from documentation"
  ]
}
```

